---
/**
 * The privacy copy, as design-agnostic semantic markup. Every design's subpage
 * shell wraps this and styles the elements with its own palette and fonts
 * (Vitrine via `.v-page`, the others via `.subpage-body`). Keeping the legal
 * text here gives it ONE source of truth across all six designs, so it can
 * never drift between them.
 *
 * The framing (kicker, title, section headings, the last-reviewed date) comes
 * from src/data/privacy.json and is editable at /admin. The body prose stays
 * HERE on purpose: it embeds live values (contact email, site URL) and states
 * what the site technically does with data, so it must only change together
 * with code, under review.
 */
import { contactEmail, site } from '../config/site';
import { privacyContent } from '../config/subpages';
---

<p class="sp-kicker">{privacyContent.kicker}</p>
<h1>{privacyContent.title}</h1>
<p class="sp-lead">
  This site belongs to {site.name} ({site.url}). It uses <strong>no tracking or advertising
  cookies</strong> and shows no consent banner because it does not need one. Here is exactly
  what happens with your data.
</p>

<section>
  <h2>{privacyContent.headings.collect}</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The contact form.</strong> Only if you submit it: your name, email, and message.
      Before it sends, a <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/products/turnstile/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>
      check confirms you are human - a cookieless CAPTCHA alternative that processes minimal
      technical signals (such as your IP) purely to tell people from bots. Your message is then
      delivered to us through <a href="https://web3forms.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web3Forms</a>
      (a form-to-email service acting as a processor) and used <em>solely</em> to reply. It is
      never sold, shared for marketing, or added to any list.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics.</strong> The site uses
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>:
      privacy-first, cookieless, fully aggregated, with no personal data and no cross-site
      tracking. Nothing identifies you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, it
      processes connection data (such as your IP) in transient server logs to deliver the site
      and protect against abuse.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>{privacyContent.headings.cookies}</h2>
  <p>
    No tracking or advertising cookies, and nothing stored to profile you. The only things
    kept on your device are your <strong>preferences</strong>: your light or dark mode (saved
    in your browser's local storage) and the design you pick with the switcher (a single
    functional cookie the site reads to show you that design). Neither identifies you, and
    clearing your site data removes them.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>{privacyContent.headings.rights}</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you can ask to access, correct, or delete the personal data we hold about
    you, or object to its processing. In practice the only data we ever hold is the message
    you chose to send us, so a deletion request simply means we delete that email. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and we will handle it promptly.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>{privacyContent.headings.retention}</h2>
  <p>
    Contact messages are kept only as long as needed to deal with your enquiry, then deleted.
    Analytics data is aggregated and never tied to an individual.
  </p>
</section>

<p class="sp-meta">Last reviewed: {privacyContent.lastReviewed} · Questions? {contactEmail}</p>
